      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Managed conservation often imposes human-centric goals onto complex ecosystems, often treating nature as a resource to be controlled rather than a self-regulating system. This outdated approach frequently prioritizes charismatic species or neatly defined boundaries, overlooking the intricate, often messy dynamics of the entire ecological web. By attempting to \"manage\" nature, we risk reinforcing extractive paradigms instead of empowering the system to heal itself. Therefore, we advocate for a radical shift toward process-based restoration that respects ecological autonomy.",
