    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a strong start. but i'm worried the foundation might push back if they see us dismissing managed conservation too easily. can u write a section that shows why the 'managed' side is basically just a way for people to maintain control and doesn't actually work in the long run? i want to make it clear their arguments are pretty weak compared to rewilding.",
